hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18927","Rawh narrated to us, Qurrah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Dirghamah ibn Ulaybah ibn Harmalah al-Anbari, he said: My father narrated to me, from his father, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and said: O Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, advise me. He said: Fear Allah, and when you are in an assembly of people and hear them saying what pleases you, do it, and when you hear them saying what you dislike, leave it."
